   "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nFixes a Git extension behavior where worktrees that users closed via **Close Other Repositories** were immediately re-discovered and re-opened during subsequent `git status`-driven worktree detection.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Filter user-closed worktrees out of `checkForWorktrees()` before queuing scans to prevent immediate re-open/flicker.\n- Fix `.git` suffix stripping in `getWorktreesFS()` to avoid over-matching (unescaped `.`) and stripping incorrect path segments.\n- Correct a misleading trace message about worktree auto-detection being skipped.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 2 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| extensions/git/src/model.ts | Prevents re-queuing scans for user-closed worktrees during automatic worktree detection; adjusts trace text. |\n| extensions/git/src/git.ts | Corrects worktree root derivation by fixing the `.git` suffix regex used when parsing worktree metadata. |\n\n\n\n",
